<title>BULGARIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>BULGARIA GOVERNMENT LIST (970424)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 24 April 97 - The Union of Democratic Forces nominated    *</p>
<p> *		   party leader Ivan Kostov as prime minister  *</p>
<p> *		   following its election victory. The	   *</p>
<p> *		   nomination must be approved by the new	*</p>
<p> *		   parliament which is expected to convene on  *</p>
<p> *		   May 5.						  *</p>
<p> *************************************************************  President**......Petar STOYANOV</p>
<p> Vice-president**.............Todor KAVALDZHIEV</p>
<p>(**Sworn in 19 Jan 97, took office 22 Jan)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING CABINET (Named 12 Feb 97)</p>
<p> Prime Minister................Stefan SOFIANSKI</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister........Alexander BOZHKOV</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Industry)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister.........Haralambi ANCHEV</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Justice)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture.....Roumen CHRISTOV</p>
<p> Culture............Emil TABAKOV</p>
<p> Defence..........Georgi ANANIEV</p>
<p> Economic Policy.............Krassimir ANGARSKI</p>
<p> Education, Science &amp; Technologies...Ivan LALOV</p>
<p> Energy...........Georgi STOILOV</p>
<p> Environment........Ivan FILIPOV</p>
<p> Finance.....Svetoslav GAVRIISKI</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...Stoyan STALEV</p>
<p> Health...............Emil TAKOV</p>
<p> Industry.........See Deputy PMs</p>
<p> Interior..........Bogomil BONEV</p>
<p> Justice..........See Deputy PMs</p>
<p> Social Care &amp; Labour...............Ivan NEIKOV</p>
<p> Territorial Development &amp; Construction.......Nikola KARADIMOV</p>
<p> Trade............Daniela BOBEVA</p>
<p> Transport.........Wilhelm KRAUS</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Parliamentary Speaker.........Blagovest SENDOV</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor.........Lyubomir FILIPOV</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			 (End government list)</p>
</text>
